---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SUPPORT_URL, GITHUB_URL, LICENSE_NAME } from "../config/site";
const desc = "Showsteps is a free, open-source Chrome extension that turns a click-through into a step-by-step guide, kept on your own computer.";
---
<Base title="About Showsteps" description={desc} path="/about/">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="page-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1>A guide maker that keeps your screenshots to itself</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Step-by-step guides are useful and tedious to make. Tools like Scribe and Tango removed the tedium and added a subscription
          and a cloud copy of every screenshot. Showsteps keeps the first part and drops the rest.
        </p>
        <h2>What it is</h2>
        <p>
          A Chrome extension. You record a task, it writes the steps, you tidy them, and you export the format you need. It works
          offline after install and has no account. The same recording can also export as a script an AI agent or a test runner can
          replay, because guides for people and instructions for agents are increasingly the same document.
        </p>
        <h2>What it is not</h2>
        <p>
          It is not a screen recorder, a hosted knowledge base or a team workspace. It records Chrome tabs only. If you need desktop
          capture, share links or comment threads, look at the paid tools. The <a href="/open-source-scribe-alternative/">comparison</a> says where
          each is ahead.
        </p>
        <h2>How it is paid for</h2>
        <p>
          It is {LICENSE_NAME} licensed and free. There is no premium tier and nothing is locked. It runs on people choosing to chip in: <a href={SUPPORT_URL}>support Showsteps here</a>. Starring the <a href={GITHUB_URL}>repo</a> or <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/issues`}>filing a bug</a> also helps.
        </p>
        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>No analytics, no accounts, no server. The <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> lists every permission and why it is needed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
